### macOS host (Darwin): bash bin/fm-linux-setup.sh --ci
fm-linux-setup.sh: this sets up Linux (WSL 2 or a server); on a Mac follow ONBOARDING.md
exit=1

### unknown flag
fm-linux-setup.sh: unknown argument: --bogus
usage: fm-linux-setup.sh [--ci]
  Takes a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 (inside WSL 2, or a server over SSH) to the point
  where a first mate can start, cloning Firstmate into ~/starship.
  Run it as your own user from your Linux home, never under /mnt/.
  --ci    skip the closing sign-in instructions (gh auth login, claude)
exit=2

### as root
fm-linux-setup.sh: run this as your own user, not root: make one with 'adduser <name>' and 'usermod -aG sudo <name>', log in as it, then run this again (ONBOARDING-linux-server.md)
exit=1

### cwd on the Windows drive (cd /mnt/c/Users/fm/proj)
fm-linux-setup.sh: /mnt/c/Users/fm/proj is on the Windows drive; run this from your Linux home (cd ~), never under /mnt/ - git, file watching and file permissions break there
exit=1

### HOME on the Windows drive (HOME=/mnt/c/Users/win)
fm-linux-setup.sh: /mnt/c/Users/win is on the Windows drive; run this from your Linux home (cd ~), never under /mnt/ - git, file watching and file permissions break there
exit=1

### ~/starship exists but is not a Firstmate clone
fm-linux-setup.sh: /home/fm/starship exists but is not a Firstmate clone; move it aside, then run this again
exit=1

